# Cobblestone raytracer — 3D Voronoi "cobbles" with sun + sky lighting.
# Based on raytracer.uiua; the per-pixel colour function was replaced with a
# vectorised 3D-Voronoi cobblestone texture, bump mapping and proper shading.
# s is the output resolution (native, no upscaling). 300 ≈ 70s natively;
# drop to ~150 for the online pad.
s  ← 300
es ← 1e-3        # ray hit threshold
ed ← 1e¯6        # normal-estimation step
# --- geometry / signed-distance scene (from the original raytracer) ---
l  ← √/+ⁿ2                       # vector length
n  ← ÷l.                         # normalise
b  ← -⊙(l-)                      # capsule/round-box piece
o  ← +⊃(l↥0)(↧0/↥)-∶⌵-⊙∶∶        # rounded object piece
k  ← 5
d  ← /↧[◌
       ∶/↧-∶5⌵.
       ∶o [1 0.05 0.2] [2.2 0.15 ¯0.5].
       ∶o [0.3 0.05 0.05] [1.5 0.2 ¯0.3].
       ∶o [0.3 0.05 0.05] [1.5 0.25 ¯0.25].
       ∶o [0.3 0.05 0.05] [1.5 0.3 ¯0.2].
       ∶o [0.3 0.05 0.05] [1.5 0.35 ¯0.15].
       ∶b 0.7 [3 0.1 ¯0.5].
       ∶b 0.3 [2.4 0.1 0.1].
       ∶b 0.1 [2 ¯0.3 ¯0.2].
       ∶b 0.2 [2 0.3 0.3].]
de ← n-⊙◌d.+×ed⊞=.⇡3∶d.          # surface normal (SDF gradient)
rm ← ⍢(d.+×⊙(:⊙.))(>es)          # sphere-trace march
r  ← ⊙◌◌ rm 1 ×0⇡3 n             # cast a ray, return hit point
p  ← r⊂2-0.5÷-1s⊂                # primary ray for pixel (i j)
# --- cobblestone texture (3D Voronoi / Worley noise) ---
Sc ← 7                           # cobbles per world unit
Nn ← ⇡27
Of ← ⍉[+¯1⌊÷9Nn  +¯1◿3⌊÷3Nn  +¯1◿3Nn]      # 27 neighbour-cell offsets
Mx ← [127.1_311.7_74.7 269.5_183.3_246.1 113.5_271.9_124.6]
Hh ← ◿1 ×43758.5453 ∿ /+ ×Mx     # 3D hash -> feature point in cell
Mc ← [0.07 0.06 0.06]            # mortar colour
St ← [0.95 0.86 0.72]            # stone base colour
Ld ← n [0.55 0.8 ¯0.4]           # light direction
Sun ← [1.05 0.95 0.78]           # warm key light
Amb ← [0.34 0.4 0.5]             # cool sky ambient
Sky ← [0.52 0.64 0.82]           # background / fog colour
# --- render ---
Hit ← ↯[×s s 3] ⊞p .⇡s           # hit point per pixel  (N×3)
Nf  ← ≡de Hit                    # surface normals      (N×3)
Q   ← ×Sc Hit
Ce  ← ≡(+Of¤) ⌊Q                 # the 27 candidate cells per point
Dv  ← ≡(-¤) Q +Ce ≡≡Hh Ce        # offsets to their feature points
Z   ← ≡≡l Dv                     # distances            (N×27)
Fa  ← ≡(/↧) Z                    # F1  (nearest)
Fb  ← ≡(⊡1⊏⍏.) Z                 # F2  (second nearest)
Cr  ← ≡(⊡⊢⍏) Z ≡≡(⊢Hh) Ce        # per-stone random value
Mr  ← ↧1 ×22 -Fa Fb              # mortar mask (1 stone, 0 in the cracks)
Tn  ← +0.45 ×0.55 Cr             # per-stone brightness
Dm  ← -1.15 ×0.6 Fa              # doming (bright centre)
Alb ← + ¤Mc × Mr - ⊞×(×Tn Dm)St ¤Mc        # albedo = mix(mortar, stone)
Bd  ← ≡n ≡(⊡⊢⍏) Z Dv             # direction out of each stone
Nb  ← ≡n + Nf ×0.45 × Mr Bd      # bump-mapped normal
Dif ← ↥0 ≡(/+×Ld) Nb             # diffuse term
Hem ← +0.5 ×0.5 ⊡1⍉Nb            # hemisphere term (normal.y)
Lit ← + ⊞×Dif Sun ⊞×Hem Amb      # combined light colour
Obj ← × Alb Lit
Fog ← ↥0↧1 ÷6 -5 ≡l Hit          # fade distant hits into the sky
↥0↧1 ↯[s s 3] + ⊞×Fog Sky × Obj -Fog 1
